# SMTP Settings for Email Notifications
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=ntkdung1206@gmail.com

# Gemini API Credentials
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Security Encryption Key
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (Postgres) — dùng làm database dùng chung, thay cho việc lưu
# src/db_store.json trực tiếp trong repo. Lấy 2 giá trị này tại:
# Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API.
#
# QUAN TRỌNG: đây là biến phía SERVER (không có tiền tố VITE_), nên KHÔNG
# bao giờ bị nhúng vào file JS công khai của trình duyệt. Dùng
# SERVICE_ROLE key (không phải anon key) vì server cần toàn quyền đọc/ghi
# và tự quản lý việc phân quyền Admin/Editor/Viewer ở tầng ứng dụng.
# Tuyệt đối không thêm tiền tố VITE_ vào 2 biến này.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret (src/server/auth.ts). Used to HMAC-sign the login
# session token issued by POST /api/login. Set this to a long random string
# in .env.local (and in Vercel Environment Variables for production) — anyone
# who knows this value can forge a valid Admin session, so treat it as a
# secret exactly like SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Protects GET /api/cron/weekly-backup (route name is legacy — it now runs
# the daily Google Drive database backup, see src/server/driveBackup.ts and
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID below; the email-based backup this route was
# originally named after was removed 2026-08-26) from being triggered by
# anyone who finds the URL. Vercel automatically sends
# `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` on its own Cron requests whenever
# this env var is set on the project — set it ONLY in Vercel Environment
# Variables (production). Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CRON_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Facebook Login OAuth (src/server/facebookSync.ts) — powers "Kết Nối
# Facebook" in Control Panel → Kết nối nền tảng → Facebook: the admin logs in
# once, this app lists every Page and Ad Account that login can access via
# Graph API, and the admin picks which ones to import into fb_pages/
# fb_ad_accounts — no more pasting a Page/Marketing API Access Token by hand.
# Same App ID/Secret also still double as the "App Token" for the debug_token
# probe that estimates token expiry (facebookSync.ts's fetchTokenExpiry) —
# that part was already optional/self-inspecting before this OAuth flow
# existed and still works the same way.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Create an app at developers.facebook.com/apps ("Business" type is
#      fine) — or reuse an existing one.
#   2. Add the "Facebook Login" product (Settings on that product, NOT
#      "Facebook Login for Business" unless you already use Business Login).
#   3. Under Facebook Login > Settings, add a Valid OAuth Redirect URI — for
#      local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/facebook/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000. That
#      exact string is FACEBOOK_REDIRECT_URI below — Meta rejects the
#      callback if it doesn't match exactly.
#   4. This app only ever reads (pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement,
#      pages_read_user_content, read_insights, ads_read — see
#      FACEBOOK_OAUTH_SCOPES in facebookSync.ts). Meta gates all of these
#      behind App Review for public use, EXCEPT for accounts added as a
#      Developer/Tester/Admin on the app while it stays in Development Mode
#      — go to App Roles > Roles and add the Facebook account(s) that will
#      actually connect here. Since this is an internal tool with one or two
#      admins doing the connecting, that's sufficient — no need to submit
#      for App Review at all.
#   5. Copy App ID / App Secret from the app's Settings > Basic page.
#
# App ID is not secret on its own, but App Secret is — treat it like
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FB_APP_ID=
FB_APP_SECRET=
FACEBOOK_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/facebook/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TikTok organic insights (src/server/tiktokSync.ts) — the TikTok half of the
# "Social Report" tab. Requires a TikTok Developer app with the Login Kit
# product added: https://developers.tiktok.com/apps
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Create an app at developers.tiktok.com/apps (or use an existing one).
#   2. Add the "Login Kit" product to the app.
#   3. Under Login Kit settings, add a Redirect URI — for local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/tiktok/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000. That
#      exact string (scheme+host+path, no trailing slash) is TIKTOK_REDIRECT_URI
#      below — TikTok rejects the callback if it doesn't match exactly.
#   4. Request these scopes for the app: user.info.basic, user.info.stats,
#      video.list. Sandbox/test-user accounts can use them immediately;
#      real accounts need TikTok's App Review to be cleared first — this can
#      take TikTok some time to approve and isn't something this app can
#      shortcut, so kick it off early rather than only right before you need
#      the real connection.
#   5. Copy Client Key / Client Secret from the app's Basic Information page.
#
# Client Key is not secret on its own (it's sent to the browser as part of
# the authorize URL), but Client Secret is — treat it like
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=
TIKTOK_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/tiktok/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TikTok Marketing API (business-api.tiktok.com) — powers "Kết Nối TikTok
# Ads" in Control Panel → Kết nối nền tảng → TikTok (src/server/
# tiktokAdsOAuth.ts): the admin logs in once, TikTok's own token-exchange
# response already lists every Advertiser that authorized this app, and the
# admin picks which ones to import into tiktok_ads_accounts — no more
# pasting an Advertiser ID + Access Token by hand. Separate app/credentials
# from the Login Kit app above (TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY/SECRET are for the
# developers.tiktok.com Organic/Login Kit app, not this one — different
# portal, different OAuth flow entirely: TikTok's Advertiser-authorization
# redirect, not Login Kit's PKCE flow).
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Create/use a developer app at business-api.tiktok.com/portal with the
#      Marketing API scopes this app actually needs: Ad Account Management
#      (to list authorized advertisers) and Reporting (to read performance —
#      this app never creates/edits campaigns, so Ads Management/Creative
#      Management aren't required, though granting them doesn't break
#      anything either).
#   2. Under the app's Basic Information, add an Advertiser redirect URL —
#      for local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/tiktok-ads/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000. That
#      exact string is TIKTOK_MARKETING_REDIRECT_URI below — TikTok rejects
#      the callback if it doesn't match exactly.
#   3. Copy App ID / Secret from the app's Basic Information page.
#   4. This app may need TikTok's review before a real (non-sandbox)
#      Advertiser can authorize it — same kind of wait as the Login Kit app's
#      review (see TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY above), kick it off early.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TIKTOK_MARKETING_APP_ID=
TIKTOK_MARKETING_APP_SECRET=
TIKTOK_MARKETING_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/tiktok-ads/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TikTok Accounts API (business-api.tiktok.com, Organic API) — TikTok Business
# Account OAuth for publishing videos, organic post insights, and comment
# management. Same developer app/App ID/Secret as TIKTOK_MARKETING_* above
# (just add the "TikTok Accounts" scope to it), but a THIRD, separate redirect
# field: the "TikTok account holder redirect URL" — configured under
# Get Started > Authorization in the portal, not the "Advertiser redirect URL"
# used for TIKTOK_MARKETING_REDIRECT_URI.
#
# Unlike every other redirect URL in this file, TikTok enforces strict format
# rules here and localhost does NOT qualify:
#   - must start with https:// (http is rejected)
#   - must NOT include a port number
#   - must be absolute and end with a trailing /
#   - must NOT contain a query string (?) or fragment (#)
#   - 10–512 characters total
# So for local dev you cannot point this at localhost:3000 like the other
# integrations — either use this project's real HTTPS deployment (below), or
# an HTTPS tunnel (e.g. ngrok/Cloudflare Tunnel) if you need to test the
# callback before deploying.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. In the same developer app as TIKTOK_MARKETING_*, add the "TikTok
#      Accounts" scope (requires the Accounts API Access Application Form —
#      see the app-permissions guide).
#   2. Under Get Started > Authorization, add a TikTok account holder
#      redirect URL:
#        https://marketing-report-v2.vercel.app/api/tiktok-accounts/oauth/callback/
#      That exact string (trailing slash included) is TIKTOK_ACCOUNTS_REDIRECT_URI
#      below.
#   3. Upload an app logo (<=512x512, JPG/JPEG/PNG) — required before the
#      "TikTok account holder authorization URL" will work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TIKTOK_ACCOUNTS_REDIRECT_URI=https://marketing-report-v2.vercel.app/api/tiktok-accounts/oauth/callback/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube organic insights (src/server/youtubeSync.ts) — the YouTube half of
# the "Social Report" tab (subscriber/view counts + per-video organic vs.
# advertising-driven views). Requires a Google Cloud OAuth Client ID:
# console.cloud.google.com
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Create (or reuse) a project at console.cloud.google.com.
#   2. APIs & Services > Library — enable "YouTube Data API v3" and
#      "YouTube Analytics API".
#   3. APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen — if the Google account is
#      part of Livotec/Karofi's Google Workspace, set User Type to
#      "Internal": skips Google's review entirely for these restricted
#      scopes and avoids the 7-day refresh_token expiry that "Testing"
#      status (External) apps get. Otherwise use External + Testing and add
#      the connecting Google account as a test user.
#   4. APIs & Services > Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID
#      > Web application. Add an Authorized redirect URI — for local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/youtube/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000. That
#      exact string is YOUTUBE_REDIRECT_URI below — Google rejects the
#      callback if it doesn't match exactly.
#   5. Copy Client ID / Client Secret from the created OAuth client.
#   6. The Google account used to connect a channel needs at least
#      "Manager" role on that channel (YouTube Studio > Settings >
#      Permissions, if it's a Brand Account with multiple managers) —
#      "Communications Manager" is NOT enough, it can't use the API.
#
# Client ID is not secret on its own, but Client Secret is — treat it like
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=
YOUTUBE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/youtube/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Website Report — GA4 + Search Console (src/server/googleWebsiteSync.ts).
# Explicitly NOT Google Ads (see GOOGLE_ADS_* below for that). Deliberately
# REUSES the OAuth Client above (YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID/YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET) —
# no separate GOOGLE_WEBSITE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET — so the only new setup on
# console.cloud.google.com is, on that SAME OAuth Client/project:
#   1. APIs & Services > Library — enable "Google Analytics Admin API",
#      "Google Analytics Data API", and "Search Console API".
#   2. APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen — add scopes
#      https://www.googleapis.com/auth/analytics.readonly and
#      https://www.googleapis.com/auth/webmasters.readonly to the existing
#      consent screen (alongside YouTube's scopes).
#   3. APIs & Services > Credentials > (the existing YouTube OAuth client) >
#      add a new Authorized redirect URI — for local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/google-website/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000. That
#      exact string is GOOGLE_WEBSITE_REDIRECT_URI below.
#   4. The Google account used to connect a brand's website needs at least
#      Viewer access on that GA4 property (Admin > Property Access Management)
#      and Full/Restricted user access on that Search Console site.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_WEBSITE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/google-website/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Ads paid campaign API (src/server/paidAdsApiSync.ts) — đồng bộ số
# liệu quảng cáo Google vào Digital Ads Report > Google. Requires:
#   - Google Ads API enabled in Google Cloud.
#   - OAuth client ID type "Web application" with redirect URI:
#       http://localhost:3000/api/google-ads/oauth/callback
#   - Google Ads Developer Token from Google Ads Manager > API Center.
#   - The Google account used in Control Panel must have access to the target
#     Customer ID (and, if using an MCC, enter that Manager ID in the UI).
# Scope requested by the app: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords
#
# Developer Token / Client Secret are server-only secrets. Never add VITE_.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_ADS_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/google-ads/oauth/callback
GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive full-database backup (src/server/driveBackup.ts) — the real
# "pg_dump equivalent" this app never had: the existing weekly email backup
# only ever covered the original report tables, never fb_pages/tiktok_*/
# youtube_*/ads_performance/audit logs etc. Runs daily, uploads a JSON dump
# of every table in supabase/schema.sql to a Google Drive folder.
#
# Deliberately a SEPARATE Google Cloud OAuth Client from YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID/
# SECRET above — this way a problem with that project (publish status,
# expiry, review) never takes down backups too. That said, you CAN reuse the
# exact same Google Cloud project/OAuth Client as YouTube if you'd rather
# not set up a second one: just add scope
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file and
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/userinfo.email to that same OAuth consent
# screen, add one more Authorized redirect URI to that same Client, and use
# its Client ID/Secret for both sets of env vars below.
#
# Setup steps (same Google Cloud Console flow as YouTube above):
#   1. console.cloud.google.com — enable "Google Drive API".
#   2. OAuth consent screen — Internal if this is a Workspace-owned project
#      (same reasoning as YouTube: skips Google's review, no 7-day expiry).
#   3. Add scopes: drive.file, userinfo.email.
#   4. Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID > Web application.
#      Add an Authorized redirect URI — for local dev:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/backup/drive/oauth/callback
#      for production, use your real domain instead of localhost:3000.
#   5. Copy Client ID / Client Secret.
#   6. In the app: Control Panel > Sao Lưu Tự Động > "Kết nối Google Drive" —
#      pick which Google account/Drive the backups land in. Optionally paste
#      a Drive folder ID (open the folder in Drive, copy the ID from the URL)
#      to keep backups out of the root; leave blank to upload to Drive root.
#
# Client ID is not secret on its own, but Client Secret is — treat it like
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/backup/drive/oauth/callback

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram push notification (src/server/telegramNotifier.ts +
# expiryNotifier.ts) — pushes the "token sắp hết hạn" warning that Control
# Panel → "Kết nối nền tảng" already shows in-app (Facebook 7 ngày / TikTok
# 30 ngày / YouTube 2 ngày trước hạn) out to a Telegram chat, so the team
# finds out even when nobody has the Control Panel open. Runs once daily as
# part of GET /api/cron/facebook-sync (see vercel.json) — no extra cron entry
# needed. Chosen over WhatsApp Business Cloud API for setup simplicity: no
# Meta Business verification, no phone number, no pre-approved message
# template.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. In Telegram, message @BotFather → /newbot → follow the prompts → copy
#      the bot token it gives you (looks like 123456789:AAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx).
#   2. Add the new bot to the group/channel that should receive alerts (or
#      just open a DM with it), then send it any message.
#   3. Get the chat ID: open
#      https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates in a browser (with your
#      real bot token) right after step 2 — look for "chat":{"id": ...} in
#      the JSON response. For a group chat this is usually a negative number.
#
# Bot token is effectively a password (whoever has it can post as this bot) —
# treat it like SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, never commit a real value.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# serper.dev (Google Search/News results via API) — powers the Keyword Rank
# Tracker and Brand SOV (search visibility) cards in Website Report's "SEO
# Tools" section (src/server/serperClient.ts/seoToolsSync.ts). UNLIKE every
# other integration in this app, this is a PAID, credit-metered API — every
# query costs money, so it's called on its own weekly cron
# (GET /api/cron/seo-tools-weekly, see vercel.json), never on a report page
# load.
#
# Credit budget this app is designed around (confirmed with the user,
# 2026-09; see seoToolsSync.ts's header comment for the exact math): ~27
# credits/week (22 unique tracked keywords for Rank Tracker + 5 SOV news
# queries) ≈ 21 months of runway on a 2500-credit free-tier signup grant.
# Changing the tracked-keyword list (supabase/schema.sql's
# keyword_rank_targets seed rows) or the cron cadence changes that math —
# re-check it against the account's actual remaining balance before doing so.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Sign up at serper.dev, copy the API key from the dashboard.
#   2. That's it — no OAuth, no redirect URI, just this one key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SERPER_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PageSpeed Insights API (src/server/technicalSeoSync.ts) — powers the
# "Technical SEO Monitor" card in Website Report's "SEO Tools" section. Free
# (25,000 requests/day with a key).
#
# The code treats this key as optional (PageSpeed Insights technically works
# without one, at a lower unauthenticated rate limit), but confirmed live
# while building this (2026-09-28): that unauthenticated shared quota is
# already exhausted globally (every caller without a key shares ONE project's
# daily quota, worldwide) — a real, unkeyed call returned HTTP 429 "Quota
# exceeded ... Queries per day" on the very first try. In practice, treat
# this key as REQUIRED, not optional, or the PageSpeed check will silently
# report "warning" (unavailable) every week instead of a real score.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. In the same Google Cloud project already used for GA4/Search Console/
#      YouTube (see GOOGLE_WEBSITE_REDIRECT_URI above), enable the
#      "PageSpeed Insights API".
#   2. Credentials → Create Credentials → API key. No OAuth, no redirect URI.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=
